& [Observation]
  + Windows optimized-release execution passed all sixteen focused workspace compiler MCP custody and bridge tests
  + the isolated llama_tool_reflection release build was then refused before experiment assertions when Application Control blocked fresh rmcp and thiserror build-script executables with operating-system error 4551
  + no failed Cantor assertion occurred in the refused Windows experiment build

& [Classification]
  + this is a host executable-identity policy decision and not evidence that Slice11 transcript behavior failed
  + successful Windows debug execution and successful Windows workspace release execution remain distinct from the blocked experiment release surface

& [ResolutionEvidence]
  + Ubuntu-24.04 WSL2 used isolated CARGO_TARGET_DIR /tmp/cantor-slice11-llama-experiment-target
  + the locked dependency graph was fetched once after the WSL cache reported http-body-util absent; no model provider or remote inference service was contacted
  + the exact locked optimized-release experiment then passed five transcript tests and three runner tests
  + a second locked offline replay against the populated isolated cache passed the same eight tests

& [Security]
  + Smart App Control Code Integrity signer trust antivirus firewall and host policy were not disabled weakened bypassed or reconfigured
  + no Windows-native optimized experiment execution is claimed
